called with its instance first"] [108 37 "// one allocation (queue 210: append grew it a second time)"] [113 4 "// method_check_args (PY7: dict.update() was a Go panic, test_ordered_dict's"] [114 4 "// CPythonBuiltinDictTests.test_update)"] [121 2 "// meth_richcompare: the same function of the same object; meth_hash not from the object's own hash"] [141 62 "// meth_repr"] [146 2 "// builtin_function_or_method's __module__ (PY6d's REQUEST): a module's function's module, a builtin's"] [147 2 "// \"builtins\", else None (pickle's whichmodule then finds the function in sys.modules)"] [163 2 "// methodobject.c's meth_reduce (PY6d's REQUEST: pickle saves a built-in function by name): a function's"] [164 2 "// qualified name, a bound method as getattr(self, name)"] [174 40 "// descr_reduce: a method descriptor by its class"] [183 3 "// CPython's \"at 0x...\", the address an identity number (asyncio's Handle reprs and their tests: PY6h's"] [184 3 "// REQUEST, queue 200)"] [193 2 "// cell([contents]): Objects/cellobject.c's cell_new, cell_repr and cell_richcompare (queue 205f: annotationlib's"] [194 2 "// _build_closure makes the stringifiers' cells)"] [215 35 "// tp_richcompare without tp_hash: hash() refuses a cell"] [225 3 "// empty cells come before anything else (cell_compare_impl)"] [251 3 "// module_repr: importlib's _module_repr once importlib is the import system (PY6b's request)"] [257 4 "// importlib's _module_repr: a module with a location is \"from\" it"] [262 2 "// module(name, doc=None), CPython's module_init; a subclass's instance (queue 205: six's _MovedItems) made empty"] [263 2 "// as new_module makes it, its __init__ (module.__init__ through super()) filling it"] [286 2 "// module_new: an uninitialized module (its dict empty), any arguments; module_init fills it"] [302 2 "// module_getsets: __annotations__ and __annotate__ (PEP 649), data descriptors before the dict"] [307 38 "// a subclass's instance: its class's data descriptors first"] [335 4 "// a subclass's instance: the generic lookup (its class's descriptors around the dict), then the"] [336 4 "// dict's __getattr__ (module_getattro)"] [351 23 "// PY6a (enum's global_enum): module_getattro's data descriptors first"] [361 5 "// 3.15 (queue 239, _Py_module_getattro_impl): a lazy import's placeholder reified in the module's dict"] [366 3 "// the type's methods (__dir__, __repr__ ...), then the module's __getattr__ (PEP 562)"] [371 4 "// a pending submodule of a lazy import (_PyImport_TryLoadLazySubmodule), then the dict again"] [387 5 "// module_get_resolved_dict_item: a lazy __getattr__ reified, unless it is resolving"] [400 2 "// module.__dir__ (module_dir, queue 223: traceback's suggestions call it): the dict's __dir__ function called,"] [401 2 "// else the dict's keys"] [421 1 "// functionNew is function(code, globals, name=None, argdefs=None, closure=None, kwdefaults=None), types.FunctionType"] [422 1 "// called: Objects/funcobject.c's func_new (its clinic's argument checks, then func_new_impl's in its order, and their"] [423 1 "// messages) over PyFunction_New (the code's name, qualname and docstring, the globals' __name__ as __module__, the"] [424 1 "// builtins from the globals' __builtins__). Queue 205f: annotationlib's FORWARDREF and STRING formats call an"] [425 1 "// __annotate__'s code with a _StringifierDict as its globals (typing.NamedTuple's annotated classes, pip's import)."] [491 2 "// _PyEval_BuiltinsFromGlobals: the globals' __builtins__ (a module its dict), else the running frame's"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[87 58] [88 39] [103 26] [115 27] [141 34] [150 31] [153 36] [157 58] [177 34] [196 38] [199 41] [252 42] [256 47] [294 28] [338 32] [344 41] [359 39] [360 32] [367 51] [377 41] [378 34] [385 40] [386 33] [392 79] [414 30] [439 12] [439 19] [448 31] [454 34] [460 34] [468 37] [481 29] [484 12] [484 19] [492 40] [493 26] [495 31] [500 26]]} (go/file "func.go" :imports [])

